---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { brandFor } from '@/config/brand';

const brand = brandFor('en');
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy policy" updated="July 2026" path="/privacidad">
  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller of the data collected through this site is Cogniplex SL (Tax ID / CIF
    B93768182), with registered office at C/ Rosselló 198, 3ª 2ª, 08008 Barcelona (Spain). You can
    contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What data we process and for what purpose</h2>
  <p>
    We process the data you voluntarily provide through the contact or assessment request form
    (name, role, email, company and the message you send us), for the purpose of handling your
    request and, where applicable, maintaining the business relationship. If you use the support
    chat, we also process the content of the conversation and any contact details you choose to
    share in it (name and email), for the sole purpose of assisting you.
  </p>

  <h2>3. The support chat</h2>
  <p>
    The chat is only activated with your consent (see the
    <a href="/en/cookies">Cookie policy</a>) and is initially handled by an automated assistant,
    identified as such in the conversation itself; you can ask to talk to a person at any time.
    Conversations are stored in our own messaging system (self-hosted Chatwoot) on a server
    contracted from Hetzner Online GmbH and located in Helsinki (Finland, EU), and are kept for a
    maximum of 12 months, unless you request their erasure earlier or they are needed for an
    ongoing relationship.
  </p>
  <p>
    To generate automated replies, the content of the conversation is sent to Anthropic PBC (USA),
    the provider of the language model, acting as a data processor under its Data Processing
    Addendum, with Standard Contractual Clauses safeguarding the international transfer; under its
    commercial terms, Anthropic does not use these conversations to train its models. We only send
    the model the conversation content and the page and language you are writing from; we do not
    send it identifying data you have not typed into the chat yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    The legal basis is your consent (when submitting the form or enabling the chat) and the
    legitimate interest of {brand.name} in responding to your request.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep form data for as long as necessary to handle your request and, where applicable, for
    the duration of the business relationship. Chat conversations are kept for a maximum of 12
    months. In both cases you can request earlier erasure.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Recipients and data processors</h2>
  <p>
    Form submissions are sent directly to our corporate email. We do not share your data with
    third parties except where legally required. To provide the service we rely on the following
    data processors:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hetzner Online GmbH</strong> (Germany): hosting of the chat messaging system, in its
      Helsinki data centre (Finland, EU).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anthropic PBC</strong> (USA): provider of the automated assistant's language model,
      under a Data Processing Addendum with Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Zoho Corporation — ZeptoMail</strong> (data in the EU): transactional email delivery,
      such as chat notifications when no one is available.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can exercise your rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction and
    portability by writing to <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>. You can also
    lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD).
  </p>

</LegalLayout>
